+## What happened to paste.create?
+
+It still works, as do `paste.open`, `paste.get`, `paste.list` and `paste.delete`: they are
+deprecated entry points backed by shared docs. A paste made with `paste.create` never changes
+and does not appear in the transparency log. Use it when you require an immutable paste.
+Use `docs.create` with `"visibility":"unlisted"` for an editable, versioned shared doc instead;
+it creates a different object kind, with the shared-doc limits and pricing.
+Use `docs.open`, `docs.read`, `docs.list` with `"kind":"paste"` and `docs.delete` for existing
+pastes. Existing paste IDs remain valid.
 
